  "slug": "coupled-unbiased-critical-regulator-4298",
  "summary": "Seven preprints pair perturbation with spatial, longitudinal, chromatin and isoform readouts, plus models of heterogeneity restoration and state transitions.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is measuring regulatory responses to perturbation with higher spatial, temporal or molecular resolution. Perturb-Tags links CRISPR perturbations to single-nucleus expression and accessibility to expose non-autonomous effects, while MolMap profiles chromatin responses to unmodified small molecules in non-crosslinked nuclei. LIFE-seq and LANCE-seq repeatedly sample living tissue, enabling longitudinal spatial transcriptomics of cortical injury and APAP-induced liver injury. FULL-seq jointly profiles accessibility and full-length transcripts, connecting promoter regulation to alternative first exon usage. Two computational works are more distant: models identify mixed feedback networks as most robust for restoring heterogeneity during self-renewal, and a single-cell foundation model (UCE) maps state bridges across 614 states. Together they emphasize within-tissue and within-individual dynamics over endpoint snapshots.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
